# <template file>:<absolute destination>
#
# configd writes every one of these as root:wheel with the default umask, so the
# `synapseidssensor fixperms` action (and the rc.d start_precmd) tighten them
# immediately afterwards:
#   sensor.conf      -> root:wheel 0640                 (flags only, no secrets)
#   sensor.token     -> _synapseids:_synapseids 0400    (the bearer token, nothing else)
#   sensor-ca.pem    -> root:wheel 0444                 (public trust material)
#   sensor-cert.pem  -> root:wheel 0444                 (public certificate)
#   sensor-key.pem   -> _synapseids:_synapseids 0400    (THE TLS PRIVATE KEY)
#
# The two 0400 entries are the reason fixperms exists: configd's umask would
# otherwise leave a freshly rendered secret world readable until somebody
# noticed.  Every caller of `template reload OPNsense/SynapseIDSSensor` runs
# fixperms straight afterwards.
sensor.conf:/usr/local/etc/synapseids/sensor.conf
sensor.token:/usr/local/etc/synapseids/sensor.token
sensor-ca.pem:/usr/local/etc/synapseids/sensor-ca.pem
sensor-cert.pem:/usr/local/etc/synapseids/sensor-cert.pem
sensor-key.pem:/usr/local/etc/synapseids/sensor-key.pem
